{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.PosSemidefDiagZero","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.PosSemidefDiagZero","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.PosDef","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.PosSemidefDiagZero.Matrix.PosSemidef.col_zero_of_diag_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.PosSemidefDiagZero.Matrix.PosSemidef.col_zero_of_diag_zero","kind":"theorem","line":198,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PosSemidefDiagZero.lean#L198-L210","doc":"**PSD col-zero from diagonal-zero**: by symmetry of PSD\nmatrices, the i-th column is also zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.PosSemidefDiagZero.Matrix.PosSemidef.row_zero_of_diag_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.PosSemidefDiagZero.Matrix.PosSemidef.row_zero_of_diag_zero","kind":"theorem","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PosSemidefDiagZero.lean#L191-L196","doc":"**PSD row-zero from diagonal-zero**: if `C_ii = 0` and `C` is\nPSD, then the i-th row is zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.PosSemidefDiagZero.Matrix.PosSemidef.entry_zero_of_diag_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.PosSemidefDiagZero.Matrix.PosSemidef.entry_zero_of_diag_zero","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PosSemidefDiagZero.lean#L155-L189","doc":"**PSD off-diagonal-zero from diagonal-zero**.\n\nFor a real PSD matrix `C`, if `C i i = 0` for some index `i`,\nthen `C i j = 0` for all `j`.\n\nPROOF: Given `C i i = 0`, set `v := single i 1 + t · single j 1`\n(canonical basis vectors).  PSD implies `v^T · C · v ≥ 0`.\nExpanding gives `2 t · C i j + t² · C j j ≥ 0` for all `t`.\nDiscriminant ≤ 0 ⟹ `(C i j)² ≤ 0 · C j j = 0` ⟹ `C i j = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.PosSemidefDiagZero.Matrix.PosSemidef.entry_sq_le_diag_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.PosSemidefDiagZero.Matrix.PosSemidef.entry_sq_le_diag_mul","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PosSemidefDiagZero.lean#L128-L153","doc":"**Cauchy–Schwarz inequality for PSD entries** (Horn–Johnson 2013\n§7.7): for any real PSD matrix `C` and indices `i, j`,\n`(C_ij)² ≤ C_ii · C_jj`.\n\nProved directly from the test-vector quadratic form: for `i ≠ j`,\n`v = x·e_i + e_j` gives `0 ≤ C_ii x² + 2 C_ij x + C_jj` for all\n`x` (PSD positivity + `quadratic_form_two_index`); a nonnegative\nreal quadratic has nonpositive discriminant (`discrim_le_zero`),\ni.e. `(2 C_ij)² − 4 C_ii C_jj ≤ 0`, whence the bound.  The\n`i = j` case is `C_ii² ≤ C_ii²`.  Previously an `axiom` pending\nthe Mathlib principal-submatrix-PSD API; now discharged. ","signatureChunk":0}]}